course: dictionary
lesson: 12311
title: Correctness: right, proper and fair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Correctness is a noun, so it names a thing, here a quality. It comes from the word correct, which means right, and the ending -ness turns it into a name. Read the sentence to find its meaning: «The teacher checked the correctness of every answer on the spelling test.» The teacher was looking to see if the answers were right.
explain: Correctness can also mean good manners. «Her correctness at the party made the grown-ups smile: she said please, thank you and waited her turn.» The clues are please, thank you and waiting, so correctness here means behaving in the proper, polite way.
explain: Some phrases use correctness with their own meaning. «Political correctness» is about avoiding words and actions that might be unfair or hurtful to groups of people. Some people praise it and others mock it, so when you meet this phrase, read the whole sentence to find out how the writer feels about it.
fact: Correctness means the quality of being right or true, with no mistakes.
fact: Correctness also means behaving in the proper, polite and accepted way.
fact: «Political correctness» means avoiding words and actions that might be unfair or hurtful to groups of people.
fact: In computing, correctness means a program does exactly what it should.
fact: Other phrases include «the correctness of the answer» and «grammatical correctness», which means following the rules of grammar.
exercise: «The teacher checked the correctness of every answer on the spelling test.» What does correctness mean here? | The colour of the pencils | How many pages the test had | How long the test took | *Whether the answers were right
exercise: Ella says correctness must mean being very loud. What does it really mean? | Running very fast | Speaking loudly and clearly | *Being right or true, with no mistakes | Being lost in a crowd
exercise: Which example shows correctness of manners? | Running down the corridor | Dropping litter on the floor | *Saying «please» and waiting your turn in the queue | Shouting across the playground
test: What does correctness mean for a computer program? | It has the most colours on the screen | It runs for the longest time | It makes the most noise | *It does exactly what it should
test: «Political correctness» means what? | Always agreeing with the teacher | Writing every word in capital letters | Saying every word as loudly as possible | *Avoiding words and actions that might be unfair or hurtful to groups of people
exam: «The class praised the correctness of Maya's working out, and she was proud.» What does correctness mean here? | Finishing first | Having the neatest handwriting | Being the quietest in class | *Having no mistakes, so the working out was right
